In this case, the expression for $w(x)$ is a quotient $\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x) = x^3$ and $v(x) = \cosh{x}.$ 

Therefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:

$$
 egin{aligned} egin{aligned}{w}^{′}(x) & = rac{{u}^{′}(x)\cdot v(x)-u(x)\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \  & = rac{({x}^{3})^{′}\cdot \operatorname{cosh}⁡x-{x}^{3}\cdot (\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)^{′}}{(\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)^{2}} \  & = rac{3{x}^{2}\cdot \operatorname{cosh}⁡x-{x}^{3}\cdot \operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x} \  & = rac{{x}^{2}(3\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-x\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\end{aligned}\end{aligned}
$$
